  "details": "We are using synched props for filming and there is an accumulative desync that is happening with props that have VRCObjectSync on them.  the longer the pickup object is held the more the desync happens.  this error gets worse with two objects being held by the same client.  \n\nError apears on NON-OWNERS \n\nError apears on worlds uploaded onto vrchat prior 1953 build.\n\nDesync was tested on an sdk 3 world.  Have not tested this on SDK2 worlds. \n\nDesync apears on all platforms. \n\nHere is a link to footage of the accumulating desync happening as it builds.  There are only three people in this world.  This is not network lag.  \n\nhttps://youtu.be/LxImKrsS3T4\n\nThe world shown in the video is wrld_9bb8b5cc-97d9-4cdf-ae25-40ac67bb6cb5\n\nWhich is included in both output logs.  Each output log is from a different client but in the instance at the same time to demonstrate error.",
